HST Office: every application chooses between tabs and separate windows (HST Writer, Sheets, Slides, Draw, PDF).
Owner request (13/11/2026): Tools > Options > HST Office > General has, under "Document Tabs", one row per
application with "Group files in one window (tabs)" (default, the behaviour so far) or "Each file in its own
window". A document follows the setting of its own application: with HST Sheets set to separate windows and
HST Writer to tabs, every spreadsheet opens in a window of its own while text documents group as tabs.
Exception: the HST Office window (the window that shows the Start Center, any document) always takes a
document opened from it as a tab: its Start Center and recent list, its "+" and the File menu of its tabs.
A document opened from outside (launchers, file manager, command line: Referer private:OpenEvent) or from a
window of an application follows the per-application setting.
Settings: Office.Common/Misc/DocumentTabsWriter, ...Calc, ...Impress, ...Draw, ...Pdf (booleans, true = tabs;
per user, lockable by administrators, the page shows the lock). They apply only while DocumentTabs is on.
Design (framework/source/services/documenttabgroup.cxx):
- chooseGroup: a window takes a new tab only when takesNewTab(): an HST Office window always; a module window
  when it accepts the module and neither its application nor the document's is set to separate windows.
  The window of the module used last is reused only for applications set to tabs; otherwise a new window.
- A window of an application set to separate windows shows no strip while it has one tab (so no "+", no
  detach; View > Move to New Window is disabled). Drop-merging a tab into such a window is refused.
- Option changes are listened to (one ConfigurationListener property per application): strips follow at
  once, new documents follow the new mode. "Apply to the open windows" on the Options page (one-time box,
  framework::DocumentTabs::applyWindowModes, run once the dialog is closed): windows of applications set
  to separate windows are split into one window per document (cascaded, through detach); windows of
  applications set to tabs are merged into the window the user works in or the one used last, the other
  documents becoming hidden tabs. Documents are only shown/hidden and re-grouped: nothing is reloaded,
  closed or saved, unsaved changes stay. HST Office windows, full-screen windows and a Start Center alone
  in a module window are left alone.
  The same runs for .uno:DocumentWindowMode with the argument ApplyToOpenWindows=true (macros, checks).
- Crash recovery: a saved window of an application now set to separate windows is restored as one window
  per document (the first one gets the saved geometry).
- View > "Tabs or Separate Windows..." (.uno:DocumentWindowMode, Writer/Calc/Impress/Draw menus, next to
  Move to New Window) opens the Options page (OptionsPageID OFA_TP_MISC); the feature search (Alt+Q) finds
  it through keywords of the bundled extension.
Taskbar identity is unchanged: module windows keep their module id, HST Office windows the Start Center id.
License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_document_window_modes.py; tests/runtime/check-document-window-modes.py (Xvfb).
